WEBVTT

00:00.330 --> 00:03.820
I'm actually X.

00:03.820 --> 00:04.940
What?!

00:04.940 --> 00:10.060
In other words, the "young man" 
who stole this from Michiko Takada...

00:10.440 --> 00:12.820
was none other than me.

00:13.130 --> 00:16.450
You absolute fools fell for my trap!

01:51.420 --> 01:55.300
That prize will be mine and mine alone!

01:51.500 --> 01:57.010
Initiative

01:57.500 --> 01:59.660
Hitomi-san, you were lying to us?

01:59.660 --> 02:00.510
For how long?

02:01.050 --> 02:02.810
From the beginning, of course.

02:02.810 --> 02:06.510
It was always my plan to take
the entire 2.1 billion for myself.

02:06.510 --> 02:08.630
For yourself?

02:09.100 --> 02:13.020
But there was no guarantee you'd 
be the last person standing...

02:14.280 --> 02:20.770
We could play this game a million times 
over and I'd always end up the winner.

02:20.770 --> 02:26.280
You see, it's no coincidence that I've 
been in the minority in every vote.

02:27.310 --> 02:31.050
But since you're such a little dunce,
 I'll spell it out for you.

02:31.430 --> 02:36.790
The night before the first game, 
I listened to your foolproof strategy.

02:37.010 --> 02:40.540
Even I had to admit it was brilliant.

02:40.540 --> 02:45.880
I'd never dreamed of taking
such an approach to win the game.

02:46.310 --> 02:50.300
But soon after, I came to 
an incredible realization...

02:50.820 --> 02:54.380
If I had two more teams like yours,

02:54.380 --> 02:58.310
I could ensure my own victory,
100% guaranteed.

02:58.310 --> 03:01.050
But how? I don't understand.

03:01.050 --> 03:02.860
There were only 22 people here.

03:02.860 --> 03:05.650
How could you form three teams of eight?

03:05.650 --> 03:08.200
You really are quite slow, aren't you?

03:08.200 --> 03:12.010
It was easy to make
 three teams out of 22...

03:12.010 --> 03:16.630
with me on all three teams!

03:19.930 --> 03:22.160
Caught on at last, have you?

03:22.160 --> 03:26.850
All three teams followed
 the same strategy:

03:27.140 --> 03:30.380
divide down the middle voting yes and no

03:30.380 --> 03:33.850
until only one member of 
the team is left standing.

03:33.850 --> 03:40.480
In other words, every member of the team 
should've had an equal shot at victory...

03:40.480 --> 03:42.600
Except I had an unseen advantage.

03:42.600 --> 03:45.520
Since I was on all of the teams,

03:45.520 --> 03:49.750
whichever answer I chose would 
always have two fewer votes!

03:50.200 --> 03:54.150
If I voted "yes," the yeses
became the minority.

03:54.150 --> 03:58.060
If I voted "no," the nos
 became the minority.

03:58.590 --> 04:02.590
Which meant I was guaranteed to win!

04:05.790 --> 04:10.010
I've been puppeteering
 this game the entire time!

04:10.010 --> 04:11.880
I don't believe it.

04:11.880 --> 04:15.280
You got everyone in the game
 to split into teams?

04:15.280 --> 04:18.270
I'll admit that it wasn't easy.

04:18.500 --> 04:21.440
The moment your team's 
discussion was over,

04:21.440 --> 04:26.280
I returned to the lobby but could only 
form one team from the people still there.

04:26.500 --> 04:30.720
I organized the remainder the next day, 
while the first game was ongoing.

04:30.720 --> 04:32.240
While the game was ongoing?

04:32.240 --> 04:33.910
No way! That isn't possible!

04:33.910 --> 04:35.800
It most certainly is.

04:35.800 --> 04:39.160
Remember what I said that night?

04:39.540 --> 04:43.820
When the game starts tomorrow, 
let's refrain from any team huddles.

04:43.820 --> 04:47.420
Instead, talk to the other players
 as much as possible.

04:48.680 --> 04:54.570
The purpose of that suggestion wasn't 
to keep our team's existence a secret.

04:54.570 --> 04:59.940
It was to keep you from realizing that 
I was putting together other teams.

04:59.940 --> 05:01.190
It can't be...

05:01.690 --> 05:06.640
And you were convinced the whole time 
that X was Number 15, remember?

05:06.640 --> 05:09.070
That was also my doing.

05:09.070 --> 05:11.670
I made sure he survived each round.

05:11.670 --> 05:15.740
By reinforcing the idea that he was X,

05:15.740 --> 05:18.200
I threw suspicion off of me!

05:20.210 --> 05:22.840
So you lied to us, too?!

05:22.840 --> 05:24.090
I certainly did!

05:24.090 --> 05:28.270
And this contract you signed 
with our team isn't valid, either?!

05:28.270 --> 05:29.420
That's right.

05:29.420 --> 05:32.600
The fact that you bought it 
is a sign of your idiocy.

05:37.280 --> 05:39.980
Violence? I'm all for it.

05:39.980 --> 05:42.020
I'm fifth-dan in karate, after all.

05:42.410 --> 05:44.040
I'm sure you're frustrated.

05:44.040 --> 05:46.270
But if you ask me,

05:46.660 --> 05:48.550
you only have yourselves to blame.

05:48.550 --> 05:50.690
Remember what the dealer said?

05:50.690 --> 05:54.660
"The one who can best control time
will be the winner of Minority Rule."

05:54.660 --> 05:58.280
I didn't sleep a wink the night
 before the first game.

05:58.280 --> 06:01.080
Then I spent the six hours 
of play time going full throttle.

06:01.080 --> 06:03.230
All to build my teams.

06:03.230 --> 06:07.050
I couldn't have forged this 
ironclad system otherwise.

06:07.050 --> 06:08.690
And what about you?

06:08.690 --> 06:11.810
You heard you had a surefire win 
and immediately let your guard down.

06:12.020 --> 06:14.810
Pathetic! You left yourselves wide open!

06:14.810 --> 06:19.970
That's why you'll always be 
sheep before the wolves!

06:20.810 --> 06:21.690
We lost...

06:22.130 --> 06:24.560
May I continue the counting of the votes?

06:24.560 --> 06:26.250
Oh, be my guest.

06:26.250 --> 06:28.300
My vote will be the only yes.

06:28.300 --> 06:30.940
The last one's obviously a no.

06:31.160 --> 06:32.990
Then I shall read out the vote.

06:36.630 --> 06:38.750
Our final vote, Number 22...

06:40.540 --> 06:41.710
"Yes"!

06:42.980 --> 06:43.950
What?!

06:45.870 --> 06:47.220
It's yes?!

06:47.220 --> 06:50.130
We have two votes for "yes" 
and two votes for "no."

06:50.130 --> 06:52.090
We will move on to another vote.

06:52.090 --> 06:53.390
Hold on!

06:53.390 --> 06:54.660
Wait just a minute!

06:54.660 --> 06:57.210
What in the world? Why did you vote yes?

06:57.210 --> 06:58.720
We had an agreement!

06:58.720 --> 07:01.220
We said that I'd vote yes 
and you'd vote no!

07:03.140 --> 07:04.470
I saw right through you.

07:05.520 --> 07:07.740
I knew that you were X,

07:08.540 --> 07:10.240
and I knew your whole little scheme.

07:10.240 --> 07:13.070
H-How could you possibly know that?

07:13.070 --> 07:17.320
I had you all convinced 
that Number 15 was X!

07:17.320 --> 07:19.740
Not me, I'm afraid.

07:19.740 --> 07:26.130
On the contrary, I was convinced 
from the start that he couldn't be X.

07:26.820 --> 07:28.350
It wasn't hard.

07:28.350 --> 07:31.380
It was obvious if you really 
considered the situation.

07:31.830 --> 07:36.380
X had stolen the 100-million-yen 
check from Michiko Takada

07:36.380 --> 07:38.640
and entered the venue right after.

07:38.640 --> 07:44.960
If Michiko Takada hadn't met me, 
she likely would've participated herself.

07:44.960 --> 07:50.000
Which means X had to have a disguise
prepared to fool Michiko Takada

07:50.000 --> 07:52.770
once she was in the building.

07:53.400 --> 07:56.520
You certainly met that criteria.

07:56.520 --> 07:59.920
You can disguise yourself 
as a man or a woman.

08:00.390 --> 08:02.320
But Number 15 didn't fit the profile.

08:02.320 --> 08:08.830
Someone hoping to disappear into
 the crowd would never wear sunglasses.

08:10.020 --> 08:13.640
It's effectively saying, 
"Hello. I'm in disguise."

08:13.640 --> 08:15.020
I see now.

08:15.740 --> 08:19.730
So, how did you see through my plot?

08:20.180 --> 08:24.930
I knew from the start that my 
strategy wasn't actually foolproof.

08:25.450 --> 08:31.120
If another team formed and tried the 
same thing, it'd wind up a stalemate.

08:31.670 --> 08:36.510
But even so, I intentionally billed
 the plan as "foolproof"

08:36.510 --> 08:39.200
to build unity among our team members.

08:39.200 --> 08:42.090
You could say it was a kind of bluff.

08:42.510 --> 08:45.280
So from the very start of the game,

08:45.280 --> 08:49.710
I kept my ear to the ground 
for any signs of another team.

08:50.410 --> 08:53.810
It was instantly clear to me
 that there was one.

08:54.210 --> 08:55.440
How did you know?

08:55.440 --> 08:57.100
Too much felt off.

08:57.350 --> 09:01.850
The atmosphere in the room 
was strangely carefree.

09:02.140 --> 09:05.410
It was like nobody felt they 
were in any danger at all.

09:06.650 --> 09:09.870
By the end of the first round,
 I was sure of it.

09:10.640 --> 09:15.060
None of the losers were distraught.

09:16.590 --> 09:19.350
They'd just landed themselves
 100 million yen in debt.

09:19.350 --> 09:21.270
Wouldn't you expect more grief?

09:21.270 --> 09:24.380
Perhaps a little kicking 
and screaming, even.

09:24.380 --> 09:26.370
Yet not a single person raised a fuss.

09:26.670 --> 09:31.890
It was as if they thought 
their safety was guaranteed.

09:32.990 --> 09:35.070
That was the moment I was certain...

09:35.070 --> 09:37.520
There was another team 
out there besides ours.

09:37.520 --> 09:41.310
At least one. 
In the worst-case scenario, two.

09:42.000 --> 09:46.780
And the real clincher came when
 Nao Kanzaki called me this morning.

09:46.780 --> 09:48.650
Huh? Me?

09:48.920 --> 09:51.140
She saw something...

09:51.450 --> 09:54.070
But it's not just me.

09:54.070 --> 09:56.810
I ran into that Number 1 fellow.

09:57.210 --> 09:59.650
He seemed nervous, too...

10:01.090 --> 10:02.590
Strange, isn't it?

10:02.590 --> 10:07.660
Why would someone who owes 
100 million yen to a shady organization

10:07.660 --> 10:11.570
willingly go right back to 
that organization's property?

10:12.920 --> 10:18.350
Most likely, he was worried his team's
survivor would take the money and run.

10:18.790 --> 10:21.680
You did a good job getting 
everyone on your side,

10:21.680 --> 10:24.810
but you should've coached them 
a little on how to act after losing.

10:24.810 --> 10:30.070
That still doesn't explain 
how you knew that I was X!

10:30.070 --> 10:33.820
No, it was very clear that you were X.

10:34.100 --> 10:37.840
You're obviously an exceptionally 
competitive person.

10:37.840 --> 10:39.770
You're level-headed 
and bursting with grit.

10:40.230 --> 10:44.480
However, when Nao Kanzaki 
first mentioned X,

10:44.480 --> 10:46.830
you lost your cool.

10:46.830 --> 10:48.760
I certainly did not.

10:48.760 --> 10:52.090
Hardly. You were shaken 
and made your sole—

10:52.090 --> 10:55.580
but unfortunately fatal—misstep.

10:55.870 --> 10:57.840
Number 15?! What a coincidence!

10:58.110 --> 11:02.520
I also thought he was behaving strangely!

11:02.520 --> 11:04.290
You did, Hitomi-san?

11:04.290 --> 11:07.050
I mean, he acts like he doesn't 
have a care in the world!

11:07.430 --> 11:13.180
If he's got a 100-million-yen check
 in his pocket, that would explain it.

11:13.410 --> 11:15.760
And how exactly was that a misstep?

11:15.760 --> 11:20.570
Nao Kanzaki had mentioned 
that X stole 100 million yen,

11:20.870 --> 11:23.820
but she never said anything about a check.

11:25.080 --> 11:30.320
Only X could have known the stolen 
money came in the form of a check.

11:30.320 --> 11:31.830
Incredible!

11:33.430 --> 11:36.580
Do you see the holes in your plot now?

11:37.500 --> 11:39.770
Don't pretend like you're so smart.

11:39.770 --> 11:41.440
You think you've won?

11:41.440 --> 11:44.810
All you did was thwart my plan!

11:44.810 --> 11:46.410
You haven't actually won!

11:46.410 --> 11:49.090
The game's back to square one! That's all!

11:49.090 --> 11:50.590
No skin off my nose!

11:51.410 --> 11:54.230
Back to square one, eh?

11:55.030 --> 11:56.310
That's right...

11:56.830 --> 11:59.050
We're right back to where we started.

11:59.610 --> 12:03.180
All four of them still have 
an equal shot at winning.

12:03.180 --> 12:07.860
Which means we only have a 25% chance.

12:08.260 --> 12:12.810
As the last vote ended in a tie, 
the game will continue.

12:12.810 --> 12:15.380
We will proceed to the next round.

12:17.370 --> 12:19.880
We must now ask the observer to leave.

12:19.880 --> 12:21.880
I don't think that's necessary just yet.

12:23.150 --> 12:27.680
Outside contact is only prohibited 
once the round begins.

12:27.680 --> 12:29.050
That is correct.

12:29.050 --> 12:30.940
Then let us choose a questioner.

12:31.830 --> 12:33.390
Number 22.

12:34.600 --> 12:35.660
Me, huh?

12:36.060 --> 12:39.520
I-I'm sorry. I'll leave 
the moment it starts.

12:41.290 --> 12:43.470
Your topic, please.

12:44.220 --> 12:45.530
Let us hear it.

12:46.800 --> 12:49.820
The most important thing in life...

12:50.540 --> 12:51.780
is money.

12:51.780 --> 12:53.390
We have our topic.

12:53.390 --> 12:56.550
"The most important thing 
in life is money."

12:56.550 --> 12:58.590
Those who agree, vote "yes."

12:58.590 --> 13:00.660
Those who disagree, vote "no."

13:00.660 --> 13:01.980
The time limit is...

13:01.980 --> 13:03.150
Wait a minute.

13:04.050 --> 13:07.540
It's obvious what my answer is.

13:07.820 --> 13:08.960
The heck?

13:08.960 --> 13:12.420
Is the most important thing
in life really money?

13:12.930 --> 13:15.960
My answer is no.

13:21.100 --> 13:22.610
Akiyama-san?!

13:22.610 --> 13:24.790
Hey, what the hell did you just do?!

13:24.790 --> 13:27.120
We're supposed to have 
six hours to think it over!

13:27.120 --> 13:29.740
I don't need all that time.

13:30.260 --> 13:34.200
Because I'm guaranteed to win.

13:35.410 --> 13:39.820
As you saw, I just voted no. 
There's no trick to it, either.

13:41.650 --> 13:43.930
See? This should serve as proof.

13:43.930 --> 13:46.620
Now that there's already a vote for no,

13:46.620 --> 13:51.760
if you want to be in the minority, 
you'll have to vote yes.

13:51.760 --> 13:58.140
But if all three of you vote yes, 
it'll put me in the minority.

13:58.390 --> 14:04.040
If you don't want me to win, a couple of
you have to bite the bullet and vote no...

14:04.470 --> 14:07.400
but whoever does is giving up the win.

14:08.140 --> 14:09.600
And I'm sure of one thing.

14:09.600 --> 14:12.860
No one here is that kind of person.

14:13.170 --> 14:16.110
Which means that I'll win.

14:17.620 --> 14:22.100
We have our first vote already, 
but I will now start the timer.

14:22.100 --> 14:24.750
The voting deadline is six hours.

14:31.230 --> 14:34.520
Akiyama-san acted so confident...

14:34.520 --> 14:37.240
but can he really win?

14:39.200 --> 14:41.250
Let's see here...

14:41.250 --> 14:43.480
There's already one vote for no,

14:43.480 --> 14:46.260
so I'll have to vote yes to win.

14:46.260 --> 14:50.190
But if the other two do the same,
Number 22 wins!

14:50.190 --> 14:51.470
I can't do that!

14:51.470 --> 14:54.610
If I vote no, I can't possibly win, either.

14:54.610 --> 14:57.170
So if Number 15 also votes no...

14:57.170 --> 14:59.650
That'll give it to Number 3!

14:59.650 --> 15:03.670
I can't do that, either!
 What do I do, damn it?!

15:04.190 --> 15:08.920
The guy who already voted
is in total control of the game!

15:08.920 --> 15:13.730
The one thing I do know is that 
with teams out the window,

15:13.730 --> 15:16.440
there's no surefire strategy.

15:16.440 --> 15:18.990
Wait, but...

15:18.990 --> 15:23.440
Even if my team's finished,
 I can just make a new one!

15:23.440 --> 15:26.230
Two people need to form an alliance.

15:26.230 --> 15:29.730
Whoever wins splits 
the prize with the other.

15:29.730 --> 15:34.450
One of them votes yes
and the other one votes no.

15:34.450 --> 15:37.660
That'd make for one yes and two nos.

15:37.660 --> 15:40.560
If the last player votes yes, it's a draw.

15:40.560 --> 15:43.620
And if they vote no, 
hoping to force a draw...

15:43.620 --> 15:47.880
This could work! 
It could totally score me the win!

15:47.880 --> 15:50.310
But the important thing
 is just that I don't lose!

15:50.990 --> 15:54.140
The question is... who do I work with?

15:55.440 --> 15:57.350
You want to ally with me?

15:57.580 --> 15:58.520
Yeah.

15:58.520 --> 16:01.420
It's true that by working together, 
we could avoid a loss...

16:01.420 --> 16:04.100
but why ask me and not Number 15?

16:04.640 --> 16:07.850
I've betrayed you once already.

16:08.220 --> 16:10.990
I can't work with that guy.

16:10.990 --> 16:16.520
This contract might not apply to you, 
but my signature's still valid!

16:16.520 --> 16:22.240
Which means I've gotta split whatever 
I win with these six other people!

16:22.510 --> 16:24.910
Number 15's in the same boat.

16:24.910 --> 16:29.060
He's gotta split his winnings 
with the six guys on his team.

16:29.680 --> 16:32.370
If Number 15 and I work together,

16:32.370 --> 16:36.490
the prize minus the fee to drop out
 would leave us 1.05 billion,

16:34.320 --> 16:40.290
<u>1.05 billion ÷ 14 people = 75 million</u>

16:36.490 --> 16:40.270
divided by fourteen... That's 75 million!

16:40.270 --> 16:43.010
We'd all end up in the red!

16:43.010 --> 16:49.090
I see. But while your plan prevents 
losing, it won't spell a win.

16:49.090 --> 16:52.140
Just look at Number 15 over there.

16:53.150 --> 16:58.150
It's hard to tell with the sunglasses, 
but he's been glancing our way.

16:58.960 --> 17:02.620
There are only three players 
here who haven't voted yet.

17:02.620 --> 17:05.310
Any coordinating we do 
will be plainly obvious.

17:05.310 --> 17:08.660
There's no way he'd ever vote no.

17:11.330 --> 17:13.660
We can't afford to rely 
on wishful thinking.

17:13.660 --> 17:16.250
We need to think up a surefire plan.

17:16.250 --> 17:17.200
I've got one.

17:18.130 --> 17:20.690
A plan that gives us a 
100% chance of winning.

17:21.400 --> 17:24.310
Oh, looks like they're getting started.

17:26.310 --> 17:27.840
It's simple.

17:27.840 --> 17:30.320
The three of us will form an alliance.

17:30.320 --> 17:32.200
That will guarantee us the vote.

17:32.200 --> 17:34.980
The winner will absolutely be one of us.

17:35.670 --> 17:37.110
Listen, man.

17:37.110 --> 17:41.320
We all know we can win 
with a three-person alliance.

17:41.570 --> 17:45.980
But your team, plus my team, 
plus Number 3... That's fifteen people!

17:45.980 --> 17:49.620
How are we splitting 
1.05 billion fifteen ways?!

17:52.230 --> 17:55.020
The prize won't be 1.05 billion.

17:55.020 --> 17:56.580
It'll be 2.1 billion.

17:56.580 --> 17:58.340
The full 2.1 billion?!

17:58.640 --> 18:01.670
After I win, I won't drop out.

18:01.670 --> 18:03.500
I'll advance to the next stage.

18:05.220 --> 18:07.210
Are you nuts?!

18:07.210 --> 18:08.170
Nope.

18:08.170 --> 18:09.730
Is he stupid?!

18:09.730 --> 18:11.990
The second game was hard enough!

18:11.990 --> 18:15.110
Can't he even conceive
 how hard the third will be?

18:15.530 --> 18:18.740
But it's a good thing he's dumb. 
I can make use of this!

18:19.280 --> 18:21.910
I just love that unyielding ambition!

18:21.910 --> 18:24.750
How manly! I'm truly in awe!

18:23.990 --> 18:24.750
However...

18:25.140 --> 18:28.370
Of course, that means 
I'll want a larger share.

18:28.640 --> 18:30.630
The total prize is 2.1 billion.

18:30.630 --> 18:33.510
As agreed, I'll pay the 
100-million-yen debts

18:33.510 --> 18:38.760
plus an extra 43.75 million for my 
teammates, Miura, and his teammates.

18:38.800 --> 18:49.140
Paying the Debts & Splitting the Money
for 15's Team + Miura's Team

18:39.720 --> 18:49.140
143.75 million per person x 13 people =

18:39.730 --> 18:42.560
That wipes 1.86875 billion from the pot.

18:40.160 --> 18:49.140
143.75 million per person x 13 people =

18:40.700 --> 18:49.140
1.86875 billion

18:43.570 --> 18:46.010
I'll keep 230 million for myself.

18:43.760 --> 18:49.140
Advance Payment to Number 15

18:44.160 --> 18:49.140
230 million

18:46.010 --> 18:49.140
The rest will go to Number 3. 
Is that acceptable?

18:49.140 --> 18:51.060
What exactly is "the rest"?

18:51.060 --> 18:52.490
It's 1.25 million.

18:52.490 --> 18:54.430
Just 1.25 million?!

18:54.430 --> 18:55.670
That's absurd!

18:55.670 --> 19:00.170
Why should he get 43.75 million,
 you get 230 million,

19:00.170 --> 19:02.780
and I get a piddly 1.25 million?!

19:03.060 --> 19:05.780
I can't even pay the 100-million-yen 
entry fee with that!

19:06.070 --> 19:07.540
But you can.

19:07.540 --> 19:11.170
You told us you've got 
a check for 100 million.

19:12.040 --> 19:15.120
You tried to sabotage the rest of us.

19:15.120 --> 19:18.390
As a traitor, you should be 
grateful to get even 1.25 million.

19:18.390 --> 19:19.800
Try showing it.

19:21.850 --> 19:24.050
And now they're at each other's throats.

19:24.050 --> 19:27.040
I refuse to accept these conditions!

19:27.040 --> 19:30.820
What's the big deal? You still 
get out of the game in the black.

19:30.820 --> 19:35.770
I at least want the same 
43.75 million that he's getting!

19:35.770 --> 19:39.020
What?! You think you're in 
a position to make demands?!

19:39.020 --> 19:40.460
It's not unreasonable!

19:40.460 --> 19:42.450
That 1.25 mil is an insult,
 pure and simple!

19:43.970 --> 19:46.220
Conflict is such an ugly thing.

19:47.520 --> 19:49.360
One hour remains.

19:49.860 --> 19:51.990
I won't change my stance.

19:51.990 --> 19:54.720
I refuse to yield a single yen.

19:57.860 --> 19:59.970
Twenty minutes remain.

20:02.220 --> 20:06.080
Ah, and now we're in a stalemate.

20:06.960 --> 20:08.900
Ten minutes remain.

20:09.230 --> 20:12.360
Listen. Why don't we 
make this round a draw?

20:12.670 --> 20:14.180
A draw?

20:14.180 --> 20:18.190
Force a draw, then resume 
during tomorrow's game.

20:18.190 --> 20:19.690
We're in no rush.

20:19.690 --> 20:23.310
Now that we're together, 
our victory is assured.

20:23.640 --> 20:26.710
The rest is just quibbling 
over the spoils.

20:27.030 --> 20:28.540
I suppose you're right.

20:28.540 --> 20:30.830
Let's make it a draw for today.

20:30.830 --> 20:33.230
Tch, I guess we'd better...

20:34.850 --> 20:36.330
Wait, you can't trick me!

20:36.610 --> 20:40.670
You're gonna pull a fast one 
and make yourself the winner!

20:40.670 --> 20:42.830
I'm clearly not!

20:42.830 --> 20:44.460
Like I'd believe you!

20:44.460 --> 20:47.870
You tried to sabotage us once.
There's no damn way—

20:47.110 --> 20:48.520
Fine, fine.

20:48.910 --> 20:50.640
Here's what we'll do.

20:50.640 --> 20:55.390
To ensure that it's a draw, 
I'll take our votes up together.

20:55.390 --> 20:56.480
Together?

20:56.480 --> 20:59.870
Each of you, give me your yes votes.

21:00.240 --> 21:02.760
I'll vote no to make it a tie.

21:02.760 --> 21:05.200
None of us will be able to win.

21:06.240 --> 21:08.990
There's no way for anyone 
to cheat like this.

21:09.400 --> 21:11.090
Nice idea!

21:11.090 --> 21:13.610
Yeah, no one can play 
the others that way.

21:13.610 --> 21:15.630
One minute remains.

21:27.270 --> 21:29.270
Voting has concluded.

21:29.270 --> 21:31.660
If you wish to observe, you may enter.

21:31.660 --> 21:33.140
Thank you so much!

21:35.450 --> 21:36.650
Akiyama-san...

21:38.680 --> 21:42.820
You three tried to make something work,
 but it fell apart in the end.

21:43.380 --> 21:47.530
I'm afraid this won't turn out 
the way you expect it to.

21:47.900 --> 21:49.880
Oh, but it will.

21:49.880 --> 21:52.920
This is a reflection of who you three are.

21:54.210 --> 21:55.740
I do pity you.

21:55.740 --> 21:58.660
You don't realize you fell for my trap.

21:58.660 --> 22:01.040
The hell's that supposed to mean?

22:01.040 --> 22:04.020
Calm down. You'll see soon enough.

22:04.900 --> 22:08.220
I will now tally the votes.

22:08.810 --> 22:12.510
What's going to happen? Akiyama-san...

23:45.020 --> 23:50.020
Next Time

23:45.020 --> 23:50.020
The Losers' Revival
